METISA PROPRIETARY LICENSE NOTICE
Draft for review by qualified intellectual-property counsel

IMPORTANT: This notice is not a certification that SaGaLabs owns all rights
in this repository, is not a worldwide-enforceability opinion, and does not
replace any license or permission granted by an upstream rights holder.

1. Scope

This proposed restriction can apply only to material for which SaGaLabs has
verified ownership or written authority to license. The repository includes
inherited firmware and third-party components. Existing copyright notices and
component-specific licenses remain in force for those materials and are not
revoked or replaced by this notice. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

2. Proposed permission model for SaGaLabs-owned material

No general license is granted by making a copy of this repository available.
Private, non-commercial use may be permitted only with prior written
authorization from the verified rights holder. Any other use, including
copying, modification, publication, redistribution, manufacture, commercial
use, or sublicensing, requires a separate written agreement signed by the
verified rights holder.

3. Conditions and reservations

Nothing in this notice transfers ownership, grants patent rights, overrides
mandatory rights under applicable law, or limits permissions already granted
under an applicable third-party license. SaGaLabs branding does not imply
ownership of upstream contributions. Rights in product names, trademarks,
hardware designs, and any registered or pending utility-model protection are
separate and are not granted here.

4. Publication hold

This file is a draft, not an operative final license. The licensing status of
the combined firmware must be reviewed before public source or binary
distribution. In particular, the repository contains a GPL version 2 license
text for HX711-related code and contradictory public-domain/LGPL notices for
MenuSystem. A qualified lawyer and the relevant upstream rights holders must
resolve the rights chain and compatibility before release.

For the upstream GPL-3.0-or-later notice present in inherited firmware, the
license text is available at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt. That
upstream grant applies only to the material covered by its notice; it is not a
blanket license for every file in this repository.